NAME
       cut - remove sections from each line of files

SYNOPSIS
       cut -f LIST [-d DELIM] [-s] [FILE]...
       cut -c LIST [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Print selected parts of lines. LIST is a comma separated list of numbers
       and ranges: N, N-, N-M, -M.

OPTIONS
       -f LIST
           select fields

       -c LIST, -b LIST
           select characters

       -d DELIM
           use DELIM instead of TAB as the field delimiter

       -s
           do not print lines without delimiters

       --complement
           select everything except LIST

       --output-delimiter=STR
           use STR between output fields

EXAMPLES
       cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd
       cut -c1-8 file

SEE ALSO
       tr(1), sort(1)
